T11:22:13Z","closed_at":"2021-06-16T11:22:13Z","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"<!-- Ignoring this template may result in your bug report getting deleted -->\r\n\r\n**Describe the bug**\r\n\r\nThe IFCLoader in the three.js editor is broken. It is not possible to load .ifc files in the three.js editor anymore.\r\n\r\nI am pretty sure this got introduced with PR #21683, as the issue looks like the web-ifc WASM file is not correctly loaded (or maybe it is not even served on a web server at all). Am I right, @agviegas ?\r\n\r\nAs I know somebody will ask eventually, the file I used is the one of the IFCLoader example (rac_advanced_sample_project.ifc), but I am confident the issue is the same for any .ifc file.\r\n\r\n**To Reproduce**\r\n\r\nSteps to reproduce the behavior:\r\n1. Open the three.js editor\r\n2. Drag and drop an .ifc file\r\n3. See error\r\n\r\n**Expected behavior**\r\n\r\nThe loaded .ifc file displays in the three.js editor.\r\n\r\n**Screenshots**\r\n\r\nHere is the output of the console.\r\n<img width=\"1195\" alt=\"Capture d’écran 2021-06-15 à 09 50 55\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/2658206/122014580-96f4b800-cdbf-11eb-8d78-e9b4fb3ec4a4.png\">\r\n\r\n**Platform:**\r\n\r\n - Device: Desktop\r\n - OS: MacOS\r\n - Browser: Safari\r\n - Three.js version: Version currently used on the editor\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"mrdoob","id":97088,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk3MDg4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/97088?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrdoob","html_url":"https://github.com/mrdoob","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrdoob/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrdoob/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrdoob/gists{/gist_id}","starre